7. STAGED IMPLEMENTATION PLAN
================================================================================

Four follow-up gates, each independently verifiable, each shipping a
narrower slice than "all three tools at once":

  Gate 15.2 — Chassis only, no rules, no MCP wiring yet.
    Scope: confirm the exact current JavaParser release against Maven
    Central; add the dependency (root dependencyManagement + module
    pom, per item 1); scaffold com.aqa.mcp.validation with RuleProfile,
    ModuleProfile, RuleProfileResolver, ValidationException, SourceUnit,
    JavaSourceScanner, BasePackages, ValidationRule, EvaluationContext,
    Violation, ModuleValidationResult, ValidationReport, and Tier-1/Tier-2
    tests for everything except the rule-set classes themselves (which
    don't exist yet). No RegressionMcpServer.java edit in this gate.
    Verify: `mvn -pl regression-mcp-server -am test`, plus a fresh
    `dependency:tree` diffed against the baseline captured in item 1.

  Gate 15.3 — regression_validate_module_boundaries end-to-end.
    Scope: MOD-001..MOD-004 in ModuleBoundaryRules, ModuleBoundariesTool,
    the one sanctioned additive RegressionMcpServer.java registration edit
    (flagged in item 2 — confirm with the user before starting this gate,
    since it touches an existing file), and its Tier-1/Tier-2/contract
    tests. Chosen first because it's the smallest rule set and proves the
    whole chassis (scanner, EvaluationContext, tool wiring, schema) against
    one real MCP tool before the other two are built on top of it.
    Verify: `mvn -pl regression-mcp-server -am test`.

  Gate 15.4 — regression_validate_framework_conventions end-to-end.
    Scope: resolve the Selenium-vs-Playwright per-module scoping question
    flagged in item 4 first (does regression-jhipster's Playwright-based UI
    layer get its own parallel rule set, or do FC-001/002/005 simply not
    fire there for now); then FC-001..FC-005 in FrameworkConventionRules,
    FrameworkConventionsTool, RegressionMcpServer.java registration, tests.
    Decide FC-004's advisory-vs-hard status explicitly in this gate rather
    than carrying the item-4 placeholder forward silently.
    Verify: `mvn -pl regression-mcp-server -am test`.

  Gate 15.5 — regression_validate_architecture end-to-end.
    Scope: ARCH-001..ARCH-004 in ArchitectureRules, ArchitectureTool,
    RegressionMcpServer.java registration, tests. Calibrate ARCH-004's
    method-count/vocabulary threshold against the two real BasePage classes
    found during grounding (jhipster's and nextjs-commerce's) rather than
    picking an arbitrary number. Revisit whether a Symbol Solver is
    genuinely needed for any of the four rules only if Tier-1 testing in
    this gate surfaces a specific, real false-positive/negative that the
    import-based heuristics in item 4 can't resolve — do not add it
    preemptively.
    Verify: `mvn -pl regression-mcp-server -am test`, plus a full reactor
    `mvn -pl regression-mcp-server -am verify` as the final gate in this
    stage.

