--------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. FC-001..005 PROPOSED RULE SET
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

FC-001 (Selenium locators): precondition = class imports org.openqa.selenium.By.
Violation = a By-typed field declared anywhere in the class that is not
private static final. Accepted exception (not a violation): a private
static method returning By for a dynamic/parameterized locator template
(real example: ProductPage.optionButton(String,String) at
regression-nextjs-commerce/.../pages/ProductPage.java:52). Verified this
exact convention already holds cleanly across ProductPage, StorefrontPage,
SearchResultsPage, HeaderComponent, CartDrawerComponent, ProductGridComponent,
BaseComponent, ComponentRoot -- real reactor is clean of FC-001 violations
today (same "clean baseline, synthetic-fixture-only" pattern as MOD-001..004).

FC-001-PW (Playwright locator fields) -- DESIGN FINDING, not a literal
mirror of FC-001: inspected LoginPage, BankAccountPage, NavigationBar,
DataTableComponent directly. Playwright Locator fields are structurally
different from Selenium By fields: a Locator is bound to a Page/Locator
instance at creation time (page.getByTestId(...), root.getByTestId(...)),
so it can never legitimately be static -- mirroring FC-001's "private
static final" literally onto Playwright would flag every correct existing
Locator field in the codebase as a false positive. The actual convention
already followed consistently by every real file inspected is: private
final Locator INSTANCE field, assigned exactly once in the constructor
(never reassigned later), with dynamic/parameterized lookups expressed as
private instance methods returning Locator (real examples:
DataTableComponent.rowByExactCellText, BankAccountPage.uniqueRowByName/
rowByName). Proposed FC-001-PW violation: a Locator-typed field that is
(a) not final, or (b) assigned outside the constructor. This needs
explicit confirmation since it's a real adaptation of the CLAUDE.md text,
not a direct translation.

FC-002 (no Thread.sleep): technology-agnostic, applies across all
profiles verbatim (Thread.sleep is a JDK call, not framework-specific).
Grepped the entire reactor for Thread.sleep -- exactly 2 occurrences,
both in the same file: regression-core/src/main/java/com/aqa/core/utils/
WaitUtils.java:19 and :41, inside WaitUtils's own bounded polling loops
(legitimate wait-abstraction implementation, not test/product code calling
Thread.sleep directly). No occurrences anywhere else in the reactor.
CORRECTION to the open item's assumption: STAGE_15_PROGRESS.md's open
items listed both WaitManager (nextjs-commerce) and WaitUtils (core) as
needing allow-listing; direct inspection shows WaitManager.java (the
Selenium WebDriverWait-based abstraction) contains zero Thread.sleep calls
itself -- it only delegates to Selenium's own WebDriverWait polling. The
real allow-list therefore needs exactly one entry:
regression-core/src/main/java/com/aqa/core/utils/WaitUtils.java. Proposed
allow-list mechanism: an explicit, reviewable Set<String> of relative file
paths in the rule class itself (same shape as ModuleBoundaryRules's
constant sets), not a runtime flag or annotation.

FC-002-PW (Playwright equivalent, forward-looking): precondition = class
imports com.microsoft.playwright.*. Violation = any call to
Page.waitForTimeout(...) or a Locator/Frame waitForTimeout overload --
Playwright's own hardcoded-wait anti-pattern, analogous in spirit to
Thread.sleep, since Playwright's actionability auto-waiting (used
throughout via assertThat(...)/click()/fill()) is meant to replace it.
Grepped for waitForTimeout -- zero occurrences anywhere in the reactor
today, so this rule has a clean baseline and needs no allow-list.

FC-003 (constructor injection, profile-agnostic): inspected LoginSteps,
UiHooks, PlaywrightManager, DriverSession as representative samples.
Every real collaborator field in the codebase is private final, assigned
exactly once in the constructor; the only non-final mutable fields found
are legitimate scenario-local state (LoginSteps.loginPage/homePage,
UiHooks.tracingStarted), not collaborators -- a naive "non-final instance
field = violation" rule would false-positive heavily on this correct,
common pattern. Proposed narrower, low-false-positive signal instead:
flag (a) any field annotated with a field-injection annotation
(@Autowired, @Inject, @jakarta.annotation.Resource /
@javax.annotation.Resource), since this codebase uses no DI framework
anywhere, or (b) any field assigned by a public/package setter method
outside the constructor. Grepped the whole reactor for @Autowired/@Inject/
@Resource: one incidental regex hit in
regression-petstore-api/.../StoreOrderTest.java, confirmed by direct read
to be JUnit's unrelated @ResourceLock, not @Resource -- so the real
baseline is genuinely zero matches. FC-003 therefore ships with a clean
baseline under this narrower signal.

FC-004 (records for value objects, advisory-only): no new inspection
needed beyond what Gate 15.1 already decided -- reconfirming here only
that it ships as advisory (non-blocking severity), per the existing
Gate 15.1 acceptance, not re-litigated.

FC-005 (no static mutable WebDriver/browser/page-object/scenario-state):
re-ran the static-field search precisely (prior broad regex needed a
look-around ripgrep doesn't support; re-ran without it). Only match
across the whole reactor: ComponentRoot.java:14 "static ComponentRoot
document(final WebDriver driver)" -- a static factory method PARAMETER,
not a mutable static field; not a violation. DriverSession
(nextjs-commerce, Selenium) and PlaywrightManager/UiScenarioContext
(jhipster, Playwright) both confirmed to hold their WebDriver/Playwright/
Browser/Page state as private instance fields, mutated only within their
own scenario-scoped lifecycle methods -- real reactor is clean of FC-005
violations today, one rule covering both technologies (the violation
shape -- a static non-final field typed WebDriver, Browser,
BrowserContext, Page, or a page-object type -- is technology-agnostic by
construction, so no separate FC-005-PW variant is needed).

Known pre-existing fixture for future ARCH-003 (Gate 15.5, not this
gate): regression-jhipster/.../ui/pages/BasePage.java:46
(assertThat(page).hasURL(expectedUrl)), and additionally now also
observed in BaseComponent.java:20 (assertThat(root).isVisible()) and
LoginPage/BankAccountPage/NavigationBar/DataTableComponent (assertions
throughout page/component classes). This is out of scope for FC-001..005
and for this gate; noted only so Gate 15.5 has a fuller fixture picture
